        "body": "One of the main reasons businesses consider cross-platform development is the ability to manage Android and iOS development through a more unified architecture.\n\nShared functionality can include:\n\nSome features may still need platform-specific development.\n\nFor example, device APIs, platform permissions, background behaviour, store requirements, biometric authentication, Bluetooth, NFC, or other hardware functionality may require different implementation work on Android and iOS.\n\nA good cross-platform architecture therefore focuses on appropriate code reuse, rather than assuming every line of code should be identical across both platforms.",
