      {
        "heading": "Build Your Speech Recognition Solution with Clickmasters",
        "body": "The supplied content does not contain a separate final CTA block, so reserve this position in the template for approved conversion copy.\n\nPrimary CTA: Book a Speech Recognition Consultation\n\nFrequently Asked Questions",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are speech recognition development services?",
        "body": "Speech recognition development services involve building or integrating software that converts spoken audio into text or machine-readable information and connects that capability with web, mobile or business applications.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is automatic speech recognition?",
        "body": "Automatic Speech Recognition, or ASR, is technology that processes spoken audio and converts it into text.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is speech-to-text?",
        "body": "Speech-to-text is the process of converting spoken language into written text using speech recognition technology.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is the difference between speech recognition and NLP?",
        "body": "Speech recognition converts audio into text, while NLP analyses language to identify meaning, entities, intent, sentiment or other information.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can speech recognition work in real time?",
        "body": "Yes. Speech recognition can process streaming audio in real time or near real time where the selected technology, infrastructure and application architecture support it.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can speech recognition process recorded audio files?",
        "body": "Yes. Recorded audio can be processed through batch transcription workflows where immediate results are unnecessary.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is speaker diarisation?",
        "body": "Speaker diarisation separates a recording into speaker segments to determine who spoke when. It does not necessarily identify the real-world identity of each speaker.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can speech recognition handle specialist terminology?",
        "body": "Depending on the selected speech technology, specialist terminology can sometimes be supported through vocabulary configuration, model adaptation, fine-tuning or transcript post-processing.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "How is speech recognition accuracy measured?",
        "body": "Word Error Rate is a common ASR metric. Evaluation should also use representative audio and consider the requirements of the application where the transcript will be used.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "What affects speech recognition accuracy?",
        "body": "Recognition performance can be affected by audio quality, background noise, accents, pronunciation, speaker overlap, vocabulary, microphone quality and model selection.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Should we build custom speech recognition or use an API?",
        "body": "Existing APIs can suit standard requirements and faster integration, while a more customised implementation may be appropriate when a project requires specialised vocabulary, greater deployment control or deeper application-specific behaviour.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can speech recognition integrate with existing software?",
        "body": "Yes. Speech recognition can often be connected with existing applications through APIs, streaming services, backend components or SDK integrations.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can speech recognition be combined with NLP?",
        "body": "Yes. After speech is transcribed, NLP can analyse the resulting text for tasks such as intent classification, entity extraction, sentiment analysis, semantic search or summarisation.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "How much does speech recognition development cost?",
        "body": "Cost depends on audio volume, real-time requirements, model or API selection, customisation, software development, integrations, infrastructure and deployment requirements.",
        "items": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "How long does speech recognition development take?",
        "body": "The timeline depends on the speech use case, audio conditions, real-time requirements, technology selection, application integration, testing and deployment scope.",
        "items": []
      }
