        "heading": "What Is Web Application Development?",
        "body": "Web application development is the process of designing, engineering, testing, deploying, and maintaining software that users access through a web browser.\n\nA modern web application can include several connected technical layers:\n\nFrontend → Backend → Database → APIs → Authentication → Integrations → Cloud Infrastructure\n\nThe frontend provides the user experience.\n\nThe backend manages application logic, data processing, permissions, integrations, and workflows.\n\nDatabases store and organise application information.\n\nAPIs allow the application to communicate with external systems and services.\n\nCloud infrastructure supports deployment, availability, performance, and growth.\n\nA successful project therefore requires more than frontend coding. The complete application needs to work as one connected system.",
