    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are web application development services?",
        "answer": "Web application development services include planning, designing, engineering, integrating, testing, deploying, maintaining, and improving browser-based software applications."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the difference between a website and a web application?",
        "answer": "A website primarily provides content and information, while a web application allows users to perform tasks, interact with data, complete workflows, manage accounts, and use software functionality through a browser."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do you build custom web applications?",
        "answer": "Yes. Custom web applications can be developed around specific user roles, workflows, integrations, data, business logic, and operational requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "What types of web applications can you develop?",
        "answer": "Web applications can include SaaS platforms, customer portals, dashboards, booking systems, marketplaces, internal business tools, workflow systems, subscription platforms, and enterprise applications."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can web applications integrate with existing systems?",
        "answer": "Yes. Web applications can integrate with CRM platforms, ERP systems, payment gateways, SaaS tools, databases, authentication providers, cloud platforms, and third-party APIs where suitable integration options are available."
      },
      {
        "question": "How much does web application development cost?",
        "answer": "The cost depends on functionality, user roles, architecture, UX/UI, backend development, databases, integrations, security, infrastructure, testing, and ongoing support. Project discovery is normally required before an accurate estimate can be prepared."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long does it take to build a web application?",
        "answer": "The timeline depends on scope and complexity. A focused MVP can be developed sooner than a large web platform involving multiple user roles, integrations, complex workflows, and extensive testing."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is a custom web application better than off-the-shelf software?",
        "answer": "Not always. Off-the-shelf software can be suitable when business requirements are standard. Custom development becomes more appropriate where unique workflows, integrations, functionality, data, or technical control are required."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can you modernise an existing web application?",
        "answer": "Yes. Existing web applications can be assessed for frontend, backend, architecture, database, performance, security, integration, and infrastructure improvements."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are web applications mobile-friendly?",
        "answer": "Web applications can be developed with responsive interfaces that adapt to desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes. The exact mobile experience depends on the application's functionality and requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do you provide web application maintenance?",
        "answer": "Yes. Maintenance can include bug fixes, security updates, dependency upgrades, performance improvements, integration changes, database optimisation, and new feature development."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I choose a web app development company?",
        "answer": "Look for relevant application experience, frontend and backend engineering capabilities, architecture expertise, API integration knowledge, security practices, QA processes, communication, case studies, and post-launch support."
      },
      {
        "question": "Build Your Custom Web Application with ClickMasters",
        "answer": "Need a SaaS platform, customer portal, dashboard, internal business application, marketplace, workflow system, or another browser-based software product? ClickMasters can help define your requirements, design the user experience, plan the architecture, develop the frontend and backend, connect your business systems, test the application, deploy it, and support its continued development."
      }
    ],
